Puzzling on the look of my slides for a while, I want to share some custom css modifications with you. 

Basic modifications can be made in the YAML header and are explained in Yihuis [presentation slides](http://slides.yihui.name/xaringan/#1) (font, code block highlighting style).

Further customisation needs to be specified in a custom .css file which is refrenced in the header. See [here](http://slides.yihui.name/xaringan/#29). 

If you have no idea about CSS (as it was for me), the following mods might be helpful:

### Inline-code 

The following code needs to be inserted in your custom CSS file. It sets a grey background for inline code. You can play around with the border-radius, padding and background. See the image below for a sample outcome. 

```css
code { /* changes inline code highlighting */
  background: #e7e8e2;
  border-radius: 3px;
  padding: 4px;
} 
```

![screenshot at jan 09 17-56-43](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/8430564/21775078/0ad3bc7a-d695-11e6-9bdd-19a9ca3b010c.png)


### Text color and linespacing of title page

Modify / split up the `.inverse h1` blocks inside your custom css file. Doing so, you can specify different text colours for the title page as the title page is based on the `.inverse` class.   
Here you can also set the linespacing `line-height` of your title page. If you have a long subtitle, it looks ugly with the defaults. 

```css
.inverse h1{
  color: #FF1B70;
}

.inverse h2, .inverse h3 {
  color: #f3f3f3;
  line-height: 1.1em;
}
```

Left: NEW (1.1em)
Right: Default (0.8em)

